.TH tensor-wasm-snapshot 1  "tensor-wasm-snapshot " 
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-snapshot \- Save or restore an instance snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm\-snapshot\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Save or restore an instance snapshot
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMAND OPTIONS
.SS save
.TP
\fB\-\-instance\fR \fI<INSTANCE>\fR
Identifier of the running instance to snapshot
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output path for the resulting `.tensor\-wasm` archive
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server (e.g. `http://localhost:8080`)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-restore\-bytes\fR \fI<MAX_RESTORE_BYTES>\fR
Maximum number of bytes the CLI will accept from the server and write to
\fI\-\-output\fR. Defaults to 256 MiB; values above the default are clamped
down so a malicious server cannot fill the operator's disk by streaming an
unbounded response body.
.TP
\fB\-\-hmac\-key\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to a 32\-byte HMAC\-SHA256 key. The file is interpreted as 64 hex characters
if it's that length (whitespace trimmed), otherwise as 32 raw bytes.
Mismatched length is rejected with a local validation error before any
network I/O. When present, the hex\-encoded key is forwarded to the server
in the \fIX\-TensorWasm\-Snapshot\-HMAC\-Key\fR HTTP header so the server can
sign the emitted archive.
.SS restore
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR
Path to the `.tensor\-wasm` archive to upload
.TP
\fB\-\-as\-instance\fR \fI<AS_INSTANCE>\fR
Identifier to assign to the restored instance
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server (e.g. `http://localhost:8080`)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-archive\-bytes\fR \fI<MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES>\fR
Maximum *on\-disk archive* size the CLI will upload, in bytes (default
256 MiB). This bounds the compressed payload only \- the decompressed
footprint is enforced server\-side and may be much larger. The deprecated
alias \fI\-\-max\-decompressed\fR is accepted for one release; prefer
\fI\-\-max\-archive\-bytes\fR in new scripts.
.TP
\fB\-\-hmac\-key\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to a 32\-byte HMAC\-SHA256 key. The file is interpreted as 64 hex characters
if it's that length (whitespace trimmed), otherwise as 32 raw bytes.
Mismatched length is rejected with a local validation error before any
network I/O. When present, the hex\-encoded key is forwarded to the server
in the \fIX\-TensorWasm\-Snapshot\-HMAC\-Key\fR HTTP header so the server can
verify the archive signature.
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-signature\fR
Refuse to restore an unsigned (v2) snapshot. Sends
\fIX\-TensorWasm\-Snapshot\-Require\-Signature: true\fR so the server rejects
any archive that lacks an HMAC trailer rather than silently accepting it.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tensor\-wasm\-snapshot\-save(1)
Capture the state of a running instance into a `.tensor\-wasm` file via the API
.TP
tensor\-wasm\-snapshot\-restore(1)
Restore an instance from a `.tensor\-wasm` archive via the API
.TP
tensor\-wasm\-snapshot\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
